<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hoechst</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hoechst was a German chemical and pharmaceutical company founded in the nineteenth century. Together with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/basf">BASF</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bayer">Bayer</a>, it led the German chemical industry, which dominated world <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/synthetic-dye">synthetic dye</a> production before the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a>. It exemplifies the industrial strength of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/german-empire">German Empire</a>.</p></div>
